# interplay_limits_all_tasks: Every task ID at once: tasks 0-255 defined over one shared address space (the same page table; one task root page each), each given the same object list of 256 buffers, all over one page; task 256 refused ("Invalid task ID"). Tasks 1-255 each run an exec that fills byte t of the page through buffer t, chained on the root FIFO one after another. Then, interleaved: child 1 holds the execs of tasks 128-255 (round 1) behind a NOP gated on the root, while the root deletes tasks 1-127 and then opens the gate; child 1's execs all run, and the task words of the deleted tasks read 0. An exec for deleted task 5 faults ("Invalid task"). Tasks 1-127 are defined again, their lists set, and run round 1. Under isolation tasks 1-255 are 255 service instances, of which 127 are ended and started again. Block calls are locked as counts and a digest.
